  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted as already signed to the claimed hypothesis direction, with 0.15 composite-unit thresholds. H97 is decisive: PTEN loss in the clean triple-intact central-predictor background and MSI-nonhigh samples has signed estimate +0.260 [0.182, 0.338], whose full interval exceeds the threshold. I accept and close it, while noting that this remains a dataset-internal conditional association. H96 is PTEN loss in adenocarcinoma excluding MSI-high: signed estimate +0.232 [0.120, 0.344]. It points in the accepted PTEN-loss stronger-dependency direction and the point estimate is well above threshold, but the lower bound is below 0.15, so it is not decisive under the interval rule. I keep it unresolved and active, especially because PTEN is boundary-sensitive and several conditional PTEN comparisons are converging. H98 and H100 are new within-MSI-high contrasts: SMARCA4 loss +0.658 [0.445, 0.871] and KEAP1 loss +0.794 [0.552, 1.037]. Despite small cell sizes, the intervals remain clearly above threshold, so I accept them with caution. H99, TP53 loss within MSI-high, is +0.301 [-0.129, 0.732]. The point estimate is in the accepted global direction but the interval is too wide and crosses threshold uncertainty; because MSI-high cells are small, this should not be read as evidence against the accepted global TP53-loss association. It is unresolved and deferred. Adenocarcinoma robustness checks are decisive for the central predictors: H29 SMARCA4-loss +0.778 [0.701, 0.854], H30 TP53-loss +0.414 [0.301, 0.527], and H31 KEAP1-loss +0.814 [0.734, 0.894]; I accept all and close them. The broad marker screen remains null or non-meaningful for APC (H101: +0.030), NF1 (H34: -0.002), and SMAD4 (H35: -0.036); all are rejected. RB1 (H33) is +0.096 [-0.002, 0.195], weakly suggestive in the positive direction but below threshold and not decisive, so I reject and close it as a global meaningful association. I request independent validation for H97 because it is a newly accepted, near-boundary PTEN claim in a clean context that could materially strengthen the PTEN pattern; the central large subtype effects are already well supported and do not need validation.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 6 appraise: New accepted evidence expands the core map. PTEN: H97 triple-intact excluding MSI-high is accepted (+0.260 [0.182,0.338]); H96 adenocarcinoma excluding MSI-high is near-threshold but unresolved (+0.232 [0.120,0.344]); H59/H86 global/MSI-nonhigh PTEN remain boundary cases. Validation requested for H97 as a rigorous check of the newly accepted clean PTEN context. MSI-high: H79 global validated accepted; H81/H87/H88/H89 internal robust accepted; new H98 and H100 accept within-MSI-high SMARCA4/KEAP1 contrasts despite small cells, while H99 TP53 within MSI-high is unresolved due wide interval. Adenocarcinoma: H29/H30/H31 accept for SMARCA4, TP53, KEAP1, strengthening subtype robustness. Broad screen now negative for APC, RB1, NF1, SMAD4, in addition to earlier negatives for KRAS, ERBB2, PIK3CA, BRCA2, MYC, CDKN2A, ARID1A, STK11, MTAP, research markers/signatures. Current best descriptive pattern: SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high -> stronger composite dependency; TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss -> weaker composite dependency; PTEN loss -> stronger dependency in several clean conditional strata, especially central-predictor-intact contexts, but not a fully decisive global threshold-crossing claim. Next priorities: run existing registered MSI-high within central-loss states H91-H94, MSI-high-by-lineage H95, lineage interactions H56-H57, remaining broad markers H37-H38, media condition H58, and PTEN conditional main effects H60/H62/H64. Avoid new high-multiplicity interaction mining unless a focused question emerges. If H97 validation is decisive, it strengthens PTEN; if conservative validation fails, preserve H97 only as accepted from original discovery with explicit caution or reassess according to combined evidence. No causal or external generalizability claims are supported.",
