  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted as already signed to the claimed hypothesis direction, with the 0.15 composite-unit threshold applied as the practical significance boundary. H97 is now independently validated and decisive. In the clean central-predictor-intact and MSI-nonhigh context, PTEN-loss has discovery signed estimate +0.260 with lower bound +0.182 and validation signed estimate +0.291 with lower bound +0.168 under the conservative validation alpha. The validation interval is wider, as expected in a conditional subgroup, but its entire interval remains above the threshold. I therefore accept and close H97. This supports a dataset-internal descriptive association between PTEN loss and stronger composite dependency in that clean conditional stratum; it is not a global claim, not causal evidence, and not evidence of single-gene specificity for the composite endpoint. H59 is the global PTEN-loss stronger-dependency claim and is due for reassessment at its validation deadline. Discovery was +0.227 with lower bound +0.131, and independent validation was +0.290 with lower bound +0.14255. The point estimates are consistently above threshold and the direction is convergent with several accepted conditional PTEN strata, but neither interval clears the 0.15 threshold and the validation lower bound is just below it. Under the stated effect-size threshold and uncertainty, this is not decisive for a global PTEN-loss association. I therefore keep H59 unresolved and close the original global comparison as a boundary case, treating refined conditional PTEN claims as the more informative route. H2 receives validation of the constructed research marker E positive claim in the negative raw direction. Discovery was +0.021 and validation +0.035, both far below the 0.15 threshold and with intervals compatible with no meaningful effect. I reject and close H2. The current scientific map in this supplied dataset is therefore: SMARCA4 loss is strongly associated with stronger composite dependency, including in adenocarcinoma, MSI-nonhigh cells, TP53-loss cells, KEAP1-loss cells, and small MSI-high cells; MSI-high status is a large, independently validated stronger-dependency association; TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are independently or internally robustly associated with weaker composite dependency; PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency in several clean conditional strata, now including an independently validated clean central-intact, MSI-nonhigh stratum, but global PTEN remains unresolved because its interval lower bounds remain at or just below the threshold. Negative findings are informative: constructed research markers and signature-marker interactions have not shown meaningful effects, and broad markers including KRAS mutation, ERBB2 amplification, PIK3CA mutation, BRCA2 loss, MYC amplification, APC mutation, RB1 loss, NF1 loss, SMAD4 loss, CDKN2A loss, ARID1A loss, STK11 loss, and MTAP loss have not provided threshold-level meaningful main effects. The most useful next work is not additional high-multiplicity mining but completing the registered conditional and interaction map: PTEN single and multiple central-predictor-intact contexts, PTEN-by-MSI and PTEN-by-subtype interactions, MSI-high effects within each central predictor state, lineage-subtype interactions for TP53 and KEAP1 loss, MSI-high-by-lineage, remaining broad markers, and the media-serum condition. All conclusions remain descriptive associations in the supplied dataset.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 6 synthesize: H97 is accepted and independently validated: PTEN loss in the clean stratum with SMARCA4, TP53, and KEAP1 intact and MSI-nonhigh is associated with stronger composite dependency; discovery +0.260 [0.182,0.338], validation +0.291 [0.168,0.414]. This is a context-specific dataset association, not global PTEN and not causal. H59 global PTEN-loss stronger-dependency remains unresolved and closed at its validation deadline: discovery +0.227 lower 0.131, validation +0.290 lower 0.14255. The convergence is scientifically suggestive, but interval uncertainty does not clear the 0.15 threshold, and accepted conditional PTEN effects do not establish a homogeneous global effect. H2 marker E positive validation is null: +0.035 [-0.052,0.121]; reject. Current supported core pattern in the supplied dataset: SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high stronger composite dependency; TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss weaker composite dependency; PTEN loss stronger dependency in clean conditional contexts, especially SMARCA4/TP53-intact, TP53/KEAP1-intact, triple-intact, KEAP1-loss, and now triple-intact excluding MSI-high with validation, but not a decisive global PTEN association. Broad negative screen includes constructed research markers/signature interactions, KRAS, ERBB2, PIK3CA, BRCA2, MYC, APC, RB1, NF1, SMAD4, CDKN2A, ARID1A, STK11, MTAP. Remaining uncertainty: global PTEN boundary; PTEN in adenocarcinoma excluding MSI-high; PTEN in MSI-nonhigh global; TP53 loss within MSI-high due small cells; registered interactions and subtype robustness checks. Next priorities: analyze existing active registered PTEN conditional and interaction claims H60, H62, H64, H70-H73; MSI-high within central predictor states H91-H94 and MSI-high-by-lineage H95; lineage interactions H56-H57 and remaining subtype contrast H73; remaining broad markers H37-H38; media condition H58; central-predictor interactions H43-H46. Avoid new high-multiplicity searches unless a focused question emerges from these registered checks. All claims remain dataset-internal descriptive associations, not causality, single-gene knockout specificity for the composite endpoint, or external generalizability."
